## The linters, before any guest

The lesson of U56, where a guest was booted three steps into a build that a
one-second linter would have stopped.

`check_zig_pages.py` in this ladder still reads the hand-kept
`zig_plug_pages.txt`, which cobblestone-qemu replaced with a derived
`zig_plug_pages.py`. **This ladder is deprecated and is not the place to fix
that**, so the live page check is cobblestone-qemu's, and running it IS the
linter because it refuses rather than guesses.

    CODEX_ROOT=cobblestone-u57rel  python3 zig_plug_pages.py   ->  ZigEmitter
    CODEX_ROOT=cobblestone-u58     python3 zig_plug_pages.py   ->  ZigEmitter

One page at both pins, consistent with U56 and with upstream never having taken
our four-page split.

Arity needed no run: the driver diff above answers it directly.

